\pard\pardeftab720\sa398\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 04 \'b7 The Decisions\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa373\partightenfactor0

\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf0 1 \'97 Mask in place, not in a modal\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f2\i\b0\fs32 \cf0 Asset:
\f1\i0  04-1-2.webp\

\f2\i Caption:
\f1\i0  Masking mode in Boards\
Porting the modal on top of the canvas was the safe option: proven, focused, with room for every control.\
I made masking a mode instead. Uploading a material image and entering masking mode focuses the image and raises a toolbar carrying all selection tools, materials, and controls. The canvas stays visible behind it.\
The reason is the same one that justifies creating Boards: masking is where a designer decides what differentiates one option from others on the canvas. A modal preserves the work underneath, but every check means multiple actions (close it, look, reopen).\

\f2\i Asset:
\f1\i0  04-1-3.webp\

\f2\i Caption:
\f1\i0  Masking toolbar in Boards\
Moving onto the canvas traded space for navigation. Selection tools nest in a dropdown and switching costs an extra click. The canvas already pans and zooms so masking\'92s navigation came off the toolbar entirely, combining two systems into one.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa373\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf0 2 \'97 Let designers leave mid-mask\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f2\i\b0\fs32 \cf0 Asset:
\f1\i0  04-2.webp\

\f2\i Caption:
\f1\i0  Snackbar appears when panning away\
The new navigation raised a new question: does the canvas stay live while masking?\
Locking it would have been safer, but a frozen canvas recreates the modal\'92s problem in a different form: the board visible, still unreachable. There\'92s little point moving masking onto the canvas if it stops working the moment you use it.\
The cost is that a designer can navigate away from the image mid-edit. The toolbar anchors to the image rather than the viewport, tracking its position and holding its size as the canvas zooms. If someone pans away, a snackbar offers to take them back.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa398\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 05 \'b7 Craft & System\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa373\partightenfactor0

\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf0 The node does three jobs\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f2\i\b0\fs32 \cf0 Asset:
\f1\i0  05-1.webp\

\f2\i Caption:
\f1\i0  Sketch to Render node with 1/3 materials masked\
The node holds up to three materials, mirrored from the toolbar, visible even when masking is closed, tracking state and letting a click reopen masking directly. It also gates generation: disabled until all materials are masked, with a running count showing what\'92s left.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa373\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf0 Anchored to the image\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f2\i\b0\fs32 \cf0 Asset:
\f1\i0  05-2.webp\

\f2\i Caption:
\f1\i0  Zoomed in canvas with a fixed toolbar size\
The toolbar anchors to the image and holds its size through zooms so it doesn\'92t get lost while panning and never renders as a four-pixel strip or oversized slab.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa373\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf0 Five controls, two exits\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f2\i\b0\fs32 \cf0 Asset:
\f1\i0  05-3.mov\

\f2\i Caption:
\f1\i0  Prototype of resetting then saving and exiting\
Undo, redo, save, reset, and close.\
Two exits: save then leave, or leave without saving.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa373\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf0 Accessibility: Interrupted, not cancelled\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f2\i\b0\fs32 \cf0 Asset:
\f1\i0  05-4.webp\

\f2\i Caption:
\f1\i0  Snackbar with return and exit paths\
Panning away doesn\'92t end masking. A snackbar keeps the mask open, offering a route back or an exit. It\'92s a status indicator, not a notification, so it stays until resolved. A self-dismissing one fails whoever takes longest to reach it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa398\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 06 \'b7 Ship & Collaboration\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f2\i\b0\fs32 \cf0 Asset:
\f1\i0  06.mov\

\f2\i Caption:
\f1\i0  Prototype of panning away, returning to image, and zooming in and out\
The behaviours that mattered here were better demonstrated than described: a toolbar that follows an image\'92s position but not its scale, a snackbar that fires when a pan carries you off the image.\
I prototyped masking mode with Claude Code and walked through it live with the Raspberry team. Questions got answered by doing rather than describing. It shipped mostly as designed, the only change being a text reset button instead of an icon.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa398\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 07 \'b7 The Outcome\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs32 \cf0 Masking data was requested but unavailable. There\'92s no mask event and no mask flag on generation. The only trace is a generic click on the toolbar labels, which misses anyone who masks by brushing and confirming. That\'92s a floor, not a count.\
The measures I\'92d want are whether designers actually moved to masking in Boards, and how often a mask session ends with panning away and returning through the snackbar \'97 the one decision here that predicted a behaviour, and so the one a number could actually settle.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa398\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 08 \'b7 Reflection\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs32 \cf0 Nesting tools in a dropdown cost a click that used to be free: switching selection tools mid-mask. I took that trade to keep the toolbar small enough for the canvas, but I\'92d revisit it. Surfacing two or three most-used tools would save a click on nearly every mask. Which two or three is a question about usage, and that data was unavailable to me.\
}